-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

NEW DEBIAN MAIN FTP SERVER

There is a new system running as Debian's main FTP server, ftp.debian.org .
The system has a T3 connection and an anonymous limit of 100 to 150, and
should provide much better service than we've recently been able to provide.
We'd like to thank the Computing College at the Georgia Institute of
Technology for their donation of the services of this system and its
Internet connection.

We'd also like to thank Central Michigan University for providing the past
home of ftp.debian.org, and I-Connect Company for providing an interim
host while we searched for a new one.

CALL FOR DEVELOPERS ON DEC ALPHA, 68K, AND INTEL 386 PLATFORMS

We are currently making progress on 68k (Atari and Amiga only, until
the kernel supports the Mac) and DEC Alpha ports of Debian. We'd like
to hear from developers who have suitable hardware and are willing to
help maintain the system on those platforms. Please e-mail the word
"subscribe" to

debian-alpha-REQUEST@lists.debian.org
	or
debian-68k-REQUEST@lists.debian.org

Make your presence known by sending e-mail to the list once you have
subscribed.

If you are interested in helping develop and maintain Debian on the Intel
i386-compatible platform, please start by installing Debian 1.1 on your
system. You can find information on that at http://www.debian.org/ . Once
you do that, please select a software package we don't presently carry, or
one from our list of help-needing packages, and tell us of your intention
to maintain that package.

	Many Thanks

	Bruce Perens
	Debian Project Leader


