	On July 4th, 1996 I happened to catch the first release of
Linux Quake being discussed.  As a regular on LinuxNET, the host of a
LinuxNET server (linux.cia.net), and a longer term fan of Linux I 
offered to help everyone out by also hosting a small site for Quake.

	My intentions were to keep this "low key" for people in the
channel.  I expected it to last a day or two.  Its has been 22 days
since I began hosting the game, and I have yet to even sit down and play
it myself in DOS or Linux due to my lack of time.

	In the past 22 days, we have given the file(s) to 8763 people
from everywhere in the world.  For the first week I noticed an average
of 20 people on at any time.  One thing this has proved for me is that
my machine is damn stable. (I have yet to receive a single complaint
from anyone about the machines speed or performance).  

	With the recent release of QuakeC, I expect another explosion
of interest in the game.  With possible updates, I assume the 9000 people
who will have hit this site by the end of the weekend will return.  

	Therefor, I am looking for interested individuals or sites who
will add quake to their ftp sites.  Please let me know so I can list your
site and full path to the game in my machine.  Unfortuantly If this high
amount of connectivity continues I will be forced to discontinue offering
quake.

- -jeff

