important details, so here it is again!

			X B a n n e r  -  v 1 . 2
		  An XDM login screen beautifier program
		Originally for Linux, but most X11 will do.
			    by Amit Margalit

Hello all!

Version 1.2 is out! Apart from the home-site, I have uploaded it to
sunsite.unc.edu:/pub/Linux/Incoming, and it should be moved from there to
/pub/Linux/X11/xutils by the time you read this.

Here are the links:

Home Page at:
http://chaos.fullerton.edu/XBanner/

FTP sites:
ftp://chaos.fullerton.edu/pub/Linux/XBanner/XBanner1.2.tar.gz
ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/X11/xutils/XBanner1.2.tar.gz

What's new in XBanner v1.2?
===========================

A new rendering effect, paste an image on the screen, check your XBanner
resource files + more:

1. A new effect called "FgGrad" that looks much like Shadow, but here,
   XBanner fills the foreground part of the text with a color gradient.
2. You can now have XBanner put an image on your screen. Particularly
   effective with Larry Ewing's Penguin Logo! (Supplied!)
3. A new program is now part of the distribution. The 'xb_check' program
   will validate your resource files for you.
4. The home page now features binaries for Linux. Both static-linked and
   dynamic-linked versions are available.
5. The home page has been changed considerably. Quite some effort was put
   into the graphics part. (Comments welcome!)

What Is XBanner?
- ----------------
Some of us have tried running XDM on their systems, as other workstations
do, and found the resulting login screen quite dull. Many commercial Un*x
implementations have their own impressive looking login screens. Linux, and
for that matter many other Un*x types do not. So??? => XBanner!

XBanner simply takes the text you tell it to, and draws it onto the screen
in a font of your choice. It renders an effect that you can choose for you
and some of these effects can look awsome. Be sure to download the pictures
in the demonstration on the web page, and view them with an external viewer,
since most browsers really make them look bad.

