DMSDOS (Doublespace/Drivespace compressed MSDOS) filesystem version 0.6.9

    - reads and writes the following compressed filesystems:
             * msdos 6.x doublespace
             * msdos 6.22 drivespace
             * win95 doublespace/drivespace
             * win95 drivespace 3 (this one with some restrictions)

    - new features since 0.6.7/0.6.8:
             * compiles as module (only for Linux kernel >= 1.3.81)
             * faster write access (delayed compression in the background)
             * defragmentation utility for compressed disks

    - new in this release:
             * kernel support for booting directly from compressed umsdos
               partition (warning: it's slow)
             * bugfixes, of course

    - still unsupported:
             * Stacker (planned)
             * Linux >= 2.0.1 (sorry, no time at the moment, please wait
               until August 1996)

    - problems:
             * Drivespace 3 access under Linux 2.0.0 (read-write) has been
               reported to cause problems in 0.6.7/0.6.8 (see docs for
               details). No problems for read-only access. I'm not 100% sure
               that this is fixed in the 0.6.9 release.

