PRESENTATION DESCRIPTION
========================
Matthew Feldt, chair of the Linux SIG, will present a detailed description
of PGP (Pretty Good Privacy).  A primary resource for the discussion comes 
from the O'Reilly & Associates book PGP, by Simson Garfinkel.

Encryption basics (using the no-mathematics explanation model), rational
for using an encryption program, obtaining PGP, compiling and using PGP
