Stella 96 is a portable emulator of the old Atari 2600 video-game console
written in C++.  It is a work-in-progress and should be consider BETA
level software.  However, you can play most Atari 2600 games with this
release.  There are five distributions:

  * Binary distribution for Linux (stella-0.3-linux.tgz)

  * Binary distribution for MS-DOS (stella03.exe)

  * Binary distribution for Power Macintosh (stella-0.3-mac.hqx)

  * Binary distribution for Windows 95 & NT (stella-0.3-win32.exe)

  * Source code distribution for Unix (stella-0.3-src.tgz)

None of these distributions contain any 2600 ROMs and please don't write
asking for ROMs because they're copyrighted!  If you own any of the
Atari 2600 Action Packs by Activision you can use those ROM images with
Stella 96.

New in this Version
===================

  * Keyboard joystick support is much better

  * Paddles are now supported via the mouse

  * Many portability issues have been resolved

Supported Systems
=================

The following systems are currently supported:

  * Linux (SVGALIB, X-Windows)

  * MS-DOS

  * Power Macintosh

  * Unix (HP/UX, Solaris, SunOS, etc...)

  * Windows 95 & NT

