I have a driver that allows you to easily manipulate single bits on
the parallel port. For instance you could hook up a bunch of leds
to your parallel port and give them different functions.

Changing an output can be as simple as the shell statement

	echo -n 1 > /dev/par1b

Reading a control line can be done from a C program with

	char val;
	read (parfd,&val,1);

This will block until the input changes value (the first
read won't block for you to get the current value when your
program starts :-).

The web page with a little more explanation and the links to 
the sources is:

