Eject version 1.3 released!
- ---------------------------

Eject version 1.3 has three purposes for CD-ROM management:

    - Ejecting the CDROM
    - Changing a CDROM driver's auto-eject setting
    - Request a switch of CD slots on an IDE/ATAPI CDROM changer

Auto-ejecting feature requires a driver which supports CDROMEJECT_SW.
Several of the Linux 2.0 cdrom drivers support this feature.

The IDE/ATAPI CDROM changer support requires Linux kernel 2.0 or higher.
Linux kernel 2.0.5 is required for support of the Sanyo 3-CD changer
(which was a popular item with some Gateway 2000 computers).  The
changer support provides the same functionality as the cdload program
included as part of the linux/Documentation/cdrom/ide-cd
Eject v1.3 is ment as an alternative to cdload but is not as a
replacement for cdload or the rest of the documentation.  Please always
take the time to read through the documentation for your specific cdrom
driver.


Eject version 1.3 has been uploaded to the incoming directory on sunsite.
It is expected to eventually be available at the following URL:

ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/utils/disk-management/eject-1.3.tar.gz

For more information on Linux CDROM support and cdrom drivers please
look at the Linux CDROM-HOWTO at
        ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/docs/HOWTO/CDROM-HOWTO
and look at information on your specific cdrom driver in the
linux/Documentation/cdrom/   directory from the Linux 2.0 kernel
source tree.


Special thanks to Jeff Tranter (Jeff_Tranter@Mitel.COM), maintainer of
the Linux eject program, for giving me permission to release this version
of the eject program.

