  4.3.  New South Wales - Hunter Valley

  o

     Name : Praetor

     Number : 049 529537 (4x28k8)

     Sysop : Matt McLeod <matt@hna.com.au>

     Notes : We have Slackware 3.0 online for download, plus Infomagic
     Sunsite and TSX-11 CD's from early this year (just before the
     release of RH 3.0.3) online, plus a modest collection of Unix
     sources, and some binaries (e.g., Netscape ATLAS beta for Linux,
     Mosaic 3.? for Linux, etc).  We also have the usual Usenet
     newsgroups for Linux, NetBSD and FreeBSD (although they aren't
     available for free - we provide low-cost net access as well).

     We also have a partial copy of NetBSD 1.1 available (just the bits
     that were uploaded - e.g., it only has a boot disk for Adaptec
     SCSI). Also has most of XFree3.1.2 (W32 server only, but most of
     the rest of it is there)

     Downloads can be made for free - login as "guest", and apply for a
     free account. Once that's been created, you can either go to the
     shell and do everything from there (cd  ftp), or select "File
     Areas" from the menu (which gives you Lynx pointing at our FTP
     archive).

     Anyone who wants to do a large download (e.g., downloading all of
     Slackware 3.0) should contact me first to arrange a time - there
     aren't any time limits, but we might get a bit annoyed if someone
     is online for 10 hours straight without at least asking first.

