A gamma release (0.28a) of SWIN a (Small/Serial/SVGAlib)-Window-System is avaiable
via EMail to petig@uni-wuppertal.de (see below)

gamma release ?
- - well, it's in daily industrial use since January 1985
        it's changing weekly !!!
        some of the really interesting features are missing
so it's somewhere between alpha and omega. ;-)
Well honestly it's in design phase (alpha) but beyond beta testing.

- - what's ready to use:
  o You can compile Programs with menus, gadgets (or what you like to call
    them) and graphical user interface. It works !
  o You can use AmigaFonts (though no WB2.0 color fonts yet), VGA fonts, MGR
    fonts, SFP-Fonts (laserjet) - with XOR, AND, OR, OVERWRITE/REPLACE and
    lots more modes.
  o You can add (graphical) icons with a single command (wimage()) - use PCX
    or (guess ...) IFF ILBM format. (or use PBMtools (planned))
  o Images and Fonts are stored in archives (not in directories) - think
    about hundred icons stored around several directories.
  o A TELNET-session or a serial connection is enough to pass graphics,
    mouse clicks etc. - It should even be enough for background file transfer
    (not fully implemented). Though you can write/read to remote files.
  o you don't need SUID root for your programs (as compared to svgalib) -
    only for the swin-executable (on linux - SCO can do without it)
  o I have programmed a standard-interface for numerical/text input in forms
    (about 60k source code) - planned for public access (If you have real
    interest ask me). It's called Sux.a. Sorry, I don't want to write an
    english documentation yet.
  o same interface for all color modes (16,256,32k,16M)(same programs)
  o floppy disk access (including formating) and printer graphics
  o automatic transfer of needed Icons/Fonts over the (TELNET/SERIAL) line
  o a standardized printer interface (with graphics)

- - what's only planned:
  o TrueColor/HiColor support
  o background file transfer
  o XWindow support (soon) / Windows support (maybe) / simple dos support
    (Not as tricky as it is now) (If anybody is interested)
  o TTF and PFB (Postscript) true type fonts (if you have documentation
    please tell me)
  o Maybe, I am going to change the copyright to GNU-copyleft - but can
    someone explain to me in a FEW words, what that means to me and you?

- - what's missing / BUGS
  o the hidden file transfer routines are only planned
  o there may be some strange configuration progblems - a serious
    need for documentation
  o there is no up to date documentation of the window functions -
    simply look in support.h and guess by name
  o swin/connect can't tell when a programm dies (core dump) the user
    might not notice (the window remains) - this is hard to overcome
  o The svga interface is not up to date - It's mere a proove of possibility
  o Scrolling will do it wrong if your screen regions are very fragmented
  o A tutorial is missing
  o not all features are documented / ready to use !

- - what will never happen (?) / is not planned
  o SWIN will never beat X - though you might prefer it over low bandwidth
    lines

- - License:
  o you can freely redistribute source code and binaries as is,
  o you can freely distribute changed code if
    - you mention the origin
    - give free of charge access to the modified source code
  * might change to GPL!

 Christof Petig                      petig@uni-wuppertal.de

****************************************   How to get ?

please EMail to petig@uni-wuppertal.de     .
Simply specify wether you
- - want a binary to look at it
- - want to help (after looking at it) and get every (pre-)release
- - want only the stable versions (like a mailing list)
- - simply ask a question

- - can read MIME or not

Feel free to ask if swin might (ever) fulfil your needs
(First hundred users are welcome - then I reply a standard form).

The source code is about 250k in size (gzip),
the binary distribution is under construction
(should be about 400k including some fonts and demo programs)


