NetKit-B-0.07 has been uploaded to ftp.uk.linux.org (in
/pub/linux/Networking/base) and sunsite.unc.edu (in
/pub/Linux/Incoming.)

This release supersedes NetKit-B-0.06. It also supersedes the
semi-functional NetKit-B.tar.gz that has been floating around the
archives.

There is no corresponding NetKit-A. NetKit-A no longer exists. Please
get the pieces individually from ftp.uk.linux.org or other sites.
NetKit-B will probably go away soon as well.

*** This release fixes serious security problems in fingerd, talkd,
*** telnetd, and rlogin, and other potential security problems in
*** rsh, rshd, and ping. It also includes "flashproofing" in talkd.

*** Users of "sliplogin" should install the most recent version
*** (presently 2.1.0, not contained in NetKit-B) due to a severe
*** security hole in most earlier versions. Sliplogin can be obtained
*** from ftp.uk.linux.org:/pub/linux/Networking/transports.

NetKit-B no longer distributes portmap, rdist, sliplogin, lpr, or
ftpd. Separately maintained versions of these can be found on
ftp.uk.linux.org.

NetKit-B-0.07 contains the following:

		biff  comsat  finger  fingerd  ftp  inetd  ping  
		rlogin  rlogind  rcp  rpcgen  rpc.rusersd  
		rpc.rwalld  rpcinfo  rsh  rshd  rusers  rwall  
		rwho  rwhod  bsdslattach  talk  talkd  telnet
		telnetd  timed

It also contains rexecd, tftp, and tftpd, which should not be
installed unless needed.

This is a source-only release. Requires libc 5.2 or higher (though 4.7
or 5.0 should work.) Should work with any kernel released within the
last year or two. Please get gcc-2.7.2 with the strength-reduce bug
fix if you don't already have it. Also requires ncurses and libtermcap
(using ncurses instead of termcap with telnet breaks telnet, sorry,
this'll be fixed in the next release.) GNU readline is optional.

Oh yes, and as you may have noticed, the maintainer has changed.
Please send questions and comments to dholland@hcs.harvard.edu.


Special thanks to Elliot Lee of Red Hat for patches and testing and
general help.

David A. Holland	dholland@hcs.harvard.edu
