I'm proud to announce the release of ifmail-2.8e-tx7.5, you can found
it on sunsite.unc.edu:/pub/Linux/incoming/ifmail-2.8e_to_2.8e-tx7.5.tgz
(the home directory is intended to be /pub/Linux/system/Fido, but it seems
that the sunsite's maintenair is on vacation :) ).

What is ifmail?
- --------------- 
Ifmail is a package that allows a Unix machine to integrate an FTN (fido-like)
network, and act as a gateway between it and usenet and/or e-mail.
It includes the gating software, an areafix, a nodediff patcher, a mailer
and a file-echo manager.

What are "tx" patches so?
- -------------------------
These are diffs against plain 2.8e version that add some functionalities.
I maintain the "tx" diffs from many sources and contributions.

What are the differences ?
- --------------------------
"tx" versions adds charset support, References: managing, support for
different Areas files for different feeds, domain#1:2/34.56 type of
adresses support, support for packet password different than session
password, support for 16 bits product code in EMSI and yoohoo,
support for incoming calls from Terminate mailers, PGP signed messages
support, better MSGID/Message-ID managements, and more.

What is new from tx7.4 ?
- ------------------------
extract of Changelog.TX :

Changes in 2.8e-tx7.5
- ---------------------
- - replaced the "-p port" option by the "-a adress:port" of Eugene Crosser.
  changed the ifcico/openport.c with author's code.
- - applyed the Eugene's patche for nodelist.c (that is replaced my bugfix in
  tx7.4 by the Eugene's one)
- - added some CHRS_* macros (traditional and mainland iso-2022 chinese)
- - I splitted iflib/kconv.c in two files: charconv.c (general stuff and eight
  bit charsets conversions) and charconv_jp.c (japanese conversions).
  charconv_cn.c (chinese) and charconv_kr.c (korean) will be added in the
  future.
- - added the macro LANG_DEFAULT, used for autodetecting charsets (as now only
  LANG_JAPAN does something). Read README.charsets for more info.
- - corrected the movereplyto code in ifgate/message.c.
- - corrected MSGID retrieval in mkftnhdr.c for <MSGID_...@...> and <ftn_...@..>
  Message-IDs.
- - Changed the way ifmail/ifnews get the local hostname (gethostname() instead
  of $HOSTNAME) and corrected a bug about that. It also checks Reply-To:
  line for localness (LEVEL < 1)
- - Added a -DDIRTY_CHRS option; it is really dirty, but sometimes necessary.
  When compiled like that a "dirtychrs" keyword is recognized in config
  files, it tells the charset to assume for packets from a given address.
  This is to by-pass the problems of nodes doing savage charset translation,
  whitout knowing the original charset, and worste, not changing the ^aCHRS
  kludges :-(
  a "-c charset" command line option is added to ifmail/ifnews, so you can
  force a given charset for a given adress you route through if you know that
  it does savage translations.
- - Added some #ifdef MIPS_* compile options for RISCos SVR4 (seems very bad to
  handle comms :) ).
