	ANNOUNCE: dial_ppp (The 9-line poem)
	------------------------------------
in:	http://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming  
soon:	http://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/system/Network/serial
also:	http://beyond.malmo.lth.se/~gps/

	Do you have to login as root, just to start the ppp link?

	Would you like someone in the office to be able to send urgent email,
	without having the root password on a Post-It note?

	Then you need dial_ppp. It allows selected users to run specific
	commands with root permissions. Other users and other commands are
	not 'exposed', so your system is still "safe".

	This is a 313 byte 'C' program, so I hope you can understand it!
	Packaged into a 12 K .tgz complete with X11 menu (./contrib/.)

	WANTED: send me your chat_script
	--------------------------------
	Hello all you ISP's, send me your chat_script, and I'll put
	them in the next release (or you can send them again, or you can
	create your own release!) 

	I can also add your name to the dial_ppp.tcl menu
	so that your customers need to do less to get in!

	The LSM
	-------
begin3
Title:             dial_ppp 
Version:           0.0.1
Entered-date:      01JUL96
Description:       An sweet and simple utility to call pppd
                   Allows selected users to bring the link up/down
