-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Etherboot-2.0 is a package containing code that can be put in a NIC
PROM to boot Linux diskless using bootp, tftp and/or NFS.

The major changes from 1.1 are support for the bzImage provided by the
new version of mknbi, some contributed programs to make test floppies
without DOS, some bug fixes and a configuration option to make ROMs
that don't rely on the INT19H hook but take control at BIOS extension
scan time.

The version was upped from 1.1 because the Linux 2.0 documentation
referred to Etherboot-2.0 and this was the easiest way to avoid
confusion.

It has been uploaded to sunsite.unc.edu and should show up at mirrors
everywhere soon.

	Ken

