-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Hello!

Until recently there was absolutely no support for AWE32 sound card under 
Linux.  I am hoping that this will change.  As some of you might recall Mr. 
Harald Hoyer (saturn@studbox.uni-stutgart.de) has recently released a 
port of OMEGA (dos module player) for Linux.

I have added an X interface (XForms) to it and enhanced its operation.  
The player which I created (ALMP) is a pre-alpha software.  It is far from 
being very good, but it demonstrates the basics of AWE32 programming.  
The original OMEGA code did not initialize the AWE32 correctly.  This bug is 
now fixed. AWE32 can now be initilized under Linux.  This also means that 
the existing Linux software which uses FM part of the card (i.e. midiplay) 
will now work with AWE32.

Even though ALMP is an unfinished package, I am hoping that it will help
developers in writing a driver for AWE32 and perhaps a MIDI player.
ALMP plus additional information on programming AWE32 can be found at:

http://ece.wpi.edu/~witek/

Thanks,

Witek

