-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

GroupKit 3.2 has been released.  GroupKit is a Tcl/Tk extension that
provides facilities for building real-time groupware applications such
as shared whiteboards, meeting tools, games, discussion tools, etc.
The package comes with over 30 sample groupware applications/demos.
Some of the facilities provided by the toolkit are:

  * multi-cast remote procedure calls
  * shared data structures with flexible concurrency control
  * a rich set of interface widgets supporting awareness of others
  * flexible and extensible support for session management

If you haven't checked out GroupKit in a while, we've added many new
example programs, including a prototype groupware web browser, several
demos of new awareness widgets, and locking support.  This version of
GroupKit has also been upgraded to run with Tcl 7.5 and Tk 4.1.

For more information, or to download GroupKit, see our WWW page:

  http://www.cpsc.ucalgary.ca/projects/grouplab/groupkit/


